WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.300 --> 00:00:06.360
Mass spectrometry can now measure the proteins inside single cells,

2
00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:07.630
one cell at a time.

3
00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:15.370
But those cells arrive without names.

4
00:00:15.370 --> 00:00:17.760
Labelled protein references are few,

5
00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:20.310
and every lab detects a different set of proteins.

6
00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:28.220
And each cell is only partly seen.

7
00:00:28.220 --> 00:00:30.070
Much of a protein matrix is empty.

8
00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:42.380
Single-cell RNA is different.

9
00:00:42.380 --> 00:00:44.100
Its atlases are large,

10
00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:45.690
and every cell in them has a name.

11
00:00:51.800 --> 00:00:55.700
VivOME learns blood cell types from labelled RNA alone,

12
00:00:55.700 --> 00:00:59.050
then reads each protein cell against that reference.

13
00:00:59.050 --> 00:01:00.440
No protein labels,

14
00:01:00.440 --> 00:01:01.700
no paired cells,

15
00:01:01.700 --> 00:01:03.300
and no retraining on your data.

16
00:01:09.800 --> 00:01:11.450
It is built for gaps:

17
00:01:11.450 --> 00:01:13.750
it knows which proteins were never measured,

18
00:01:13.750 --> 00:01:15.730
scales each one within your file,

19
00:01:15.730 --> 00:01:17.990
and asks 5 encoders to answer together.

20
00:01:23.800 --> 00:01:27.730
Every cell gets the most precise answer the evidence allows:

21
00:01:27.730 --> 00:01:28.680
a cell type,

22
00:01:28.680 --> 00:01:29.350
its group,

23
00:01:29.350 --> 00:01:30.090
its lineage,

24
00:01:30.090 --> 00:01:31.080
or no answer,

25
00:01:31.080 --> 00:01:32.030
and the reason why.

26
00:01:37.800 --> 00:01:40.300
Its best guess adds a second opinion,

27
00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:42.960
used only when your file agrees with the encoder.

28
00:01:49.800 --> 00:01:51.730
On real blood protein data,

29
00:01:51.730 --> 00:01:53.660
here is how often it answers,

30
00:01:53.660 --> 00:01:55.620
and how often those answers are right.

31
00:02:08.800 --> 00:02:10.450
Against established methods,

32
00:02:10.450 --> 00:02:12.090
on real protein data,

33
00:02:12.090 --> 00:02:14.870
it is level with the best and ahead of the rest.

34
00:02:14.870 --> 00:02:15.990
Where it is still weak,

35
00:02:15.990 --> 00:02:16.690
it says so.

36
00:02:27.800 --> 00:02:29.270
It runs online.

37
00:02:29.270 --> 00:02:31.360
Send your file from the Atlas page,

38
00:02:31.360 --> 00:02:32.960
and your cells land on the map,

39
00:02:32.960 --> 00:02:33.940
each with its answer.

40
00:02:41.800 --> 00:02:44.140
Bring your protein cells up into the light.

41
00:02:44.140 --> 00:02:44.900
VivOME:

42
00:02:44.900 --> 00:02:46.730
no cell placed without evidence.
